            <ArticleTitle>Headaches in children. Cause for parental concern but commonly benign.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>195-9, 202</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Headaches in children are usually a benign symptom, but they can generate much anxiety in parents. The physician can alleviate this by following a thorough and informed approach to diagnosis and by offering simple, straightforward treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
